@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Notice</PageTitle>

<main class="policy-page">
    <h1>Rustles Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: June 5, 2026</p>

    <section>
        <h2>What Rustles is</h2>
        <p>
            Rustles is a location-linked public chat service. You create an account, allow your browser to share your
            current location for municipality resolution, and then participate in the chat for that municipality.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Data we use</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Account data: email address, permanent username, and authentication data needed to sign in.</li>
            <li>Registration records: your 16+ self-attestation and acceptance of the terms and privacy notice.</li>
            <li>Location input: live browser location used to resolve your municipality. Rustles does not store raw location coordinates as chat history.</li>
            <li>Chat data: messages you send, replies, emoji reaction events, reaction counts, timestamps, display names, and municipality room names.</li>
            <li>Moderation data: limited records for deleted messages and municipality-specific chat bans.</li>
            <li>Authentication cookies: strictly necessary cookies used to keep you signed in and protect account actions.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>How we use data</h2>
        <p>
            We use account data to create and secure accounts, location input to place you in the correct municipality
            chat, and chat data to show messages, replies, reaction counts, active pinned messages, and recent room
            history. We use registration records to confirm that the account creation requirements were completed, and
            moderation data to enforce chat rules in a municipality.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Public chat warning</h2>
        <p>
            Municipality chat is public within the assigned municipality room. Other users in that room can read what
            you post and may copy, screenshot, record, or otherwise keep it outside Rustles. Do not post sensitive,
            private, or identifying information unless you are prepared for other people to retain it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
        <p>
            Account data is kept while your account exists. Chat messages and reactions are stored so the service can
            provide recent chat history, reactions, replies, and pinned-message behavior. Moderation records are kept as
            needed to enforce chat rules. You can request a download of your account-related data or delete your account
            from account settings.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
            You can choose not to share browser location, but municipality chat will not work without it. You can
            download your data or delete your account from the personal-data section of account settings.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            Rustles uses authentication cookies that are strictly necessary for signing in, staying signed in, and
            protecting account actions. Rustles does not use advertising cookies or analytics cookies in this build.
        </p>
    </section>
</main>
